   <text:p text:style-name="P3"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oY3BrpoVbGI&amp;list=PLoDMmx9LIxpPcT2qrXQXAkda5pcvuWIdh" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Jesus calms the storm – in the Juni Kuin language of Peru</text:span></text:a></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:line-break/>The videos are MP4 files which can be shared with others, uploaded to YouTube or Vimeo, or integrated within a Scripture app.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list xml:id="list181652486039476" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum17">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:h text:style-name="P47" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc112848938"/><text:soft-page-break/>What resources do I need to create a slideshow video?<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc112848938"/></text:h>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">You will need:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum14">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P50">A Scripture App Builder <text:span text:style-name="T11">app project with audio and timing files</text:span>.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P49">A set of predefined <text:span text:style-name="T11">slideshow video templates</text:span>: we will show you how to obtain these in the next section. They contain all the images for the video, together with instructions on which portions of Scripture to use, where to pan and zoom and where to move from one slide to another.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list text:continue-list="list181652486039476" text:style-name="WWNum17">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:h text:style-name="P47" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc112848939"/>What slideshow templates are currently available?<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc112848939"/></text:h>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Available slideshow video templates include:</text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table1" table:style-name="Table1">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table1.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table1.B"/>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Matthew</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">3 videos (selected stories)</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Mark</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">9 videos (selected stories)</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Luke</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">6 videos (selected stories)</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">John</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">43 videos <text:s/>(complete book)</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Acts</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">4 videos (selected stories)</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table1.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Jonah</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table1.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">1 video</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list xml:id="list181651849311314" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum17">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:h text:style-name="P44" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc112848940"/>Setting up slideshow videos<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc112848940"/> </text:h>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Before you create your first video, you will need to do two things:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum15">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P51">Download the slideshow video templates.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P51">Install LibreOffice.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list xml:id="list181651272957513" text:continue-list="list181651849311314" text:style-name="WWNum17">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:h text:style-name="P48" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc112848941"/>Downloading slideshow video templates<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc112848941"/></text:h>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The video templates contain sets of images for each video, together with instructions on which portions of Scripture to use, where to pan and zoom and where to move from one slide to another. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">To download the templates:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum20">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P52"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T4">In Scripture App Builder, go to </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T12">Tools</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T12">Settings </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T12">Slideshows</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14"> <text:line-break/>(or if using a Mac, Scripture App Builder </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14"> Preferences </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T13"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14"> Slideshows)</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Picture 10" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6.2681in" svg:height="4.5346in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
