    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">The transitions between slides are not as critical, but the timing accuracy is particularly important at the start and the end of a video. For example, if you are making a video on the Visit of the Magi (Matthew 2:1-23), you will need to make sure that the timings are accurate for the start of verse 1 and the end of verse 23.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Use <text:span text:style-name="T11">Fine Tune Timings</text:span> to verify that the timings are correct.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:list xml:id="list181650810834624" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="WWNum17">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:h text:style-name="P46" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc112848944"/>Running the Create Slideshow Wizard<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc112848944"/></text:h>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P26"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P28">To use the Create Slideshow Wizard to make a video:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="WWNum19">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P57">Right-click on a book collection and select <text:span text:style-name="T11">Create Slideshow Videos…</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
